Keyed mutex fixes for cross-process sharing under Wine (SteamVR compositor, vrlink, games):
- acquire honors its timeout (Wine's D3DKMTAcquireKeyedMutex returns STATUS_TIMEOUT at once) and sleeps on the
  shared event between attempts instead of busy polling;
- an importing process waits for the releasing device's GPU work on acquire (consumers that sync on one device and
  read on another saw stale frames); dxgi.keyedMutexWaitOnAcquire = false turns it off;
- committed work is drained at process exit so a released frame is not lost.

